description:
Design a circuit that functions as a SOS (Save Our Ship) LED flasher. It utilizes a clock signal to create a timing mechanism, where the LED toggles its state every 50 million clock cycles when the input `sos` is asserted high. If the `sos` input is low, the timer resets, and the LED remains off. This module is intended for signaling distress or alerts using a specific flashing pattern.
module top_module(
input wire clk,
input wire sos,
output wire sos_led
);

code:
module top_module(
input wire clk,
input wire sos,
output wire sos_led
);reg [26:0] timer = 0;
reg timer2 = 0;

assign sos_led = timer2;

always @(posedge clk) begin
    if(!sos) begin
        timer <= 0;
        timer2 <= 0; end
    else begin
        if (timer >= 50000000) begin 
        timer2 <= ~timer2;  
        timer <= 0; end
        else timer <= timer + 1; end
end
endmodule

