description:
Design a 4-bit up counter with asynchronous reset and load capabilities. On each rising edge of the clock, if the reset signal is asserted, the counter resets to zero. If the enable signal is active, the counter increments by one. If the load signal is asserted, the counter is loaded with the value provided on the `load_val` input.
module top_module(
    input clk, rst, en, load,
    input [3:0] load_val,
    output reg [3:0] count
);

code:
module top_module(
    input clk, rst, en, load,
    input [3:0] load_val,
    output reg [3:0] count
);always @(posedge clk or posedge rst)
begin
    if (rst)
        count <= 4'b0;
    else if (en)
        count <= count + 4'b1;
    else if (load)
        count <= load_val;
end

endmodule

