Design a 2-to-4 decoder circuit with a 16-bit output, where the output corresponds to the input selection. The decoder takes a 2-bit selection input 'sel' and produces a 16-bit output 'out', where one of the bits is set to LOW (0) based on the value of 'sel', effectively enabling one of four possible outputs while the remaining bits are set to HIGH (1). Specifically, for each selection (00, 01, 10, 11), a different bit within the 16-bit output is driven LOW, enabling unique signaling based on the selected input.
