Design a 4-bit multiplier that computes the product of two 4-bit inputs, producing an 8-bit output. The module employs a sequential approach, where intermediate results of partial products are calculated based on the individual bits of the second input, shifting them appropriately and accumulating the results. The final output includes a parity bit as the most significant bit, ensuring the output is both the product and includes correctness verification.
