description:
Design a finite state machine (FSM) that operates based on a 4-bit input to determine its current state and generate a 2-bit output. The FSM has three distinct states (S0, S1, S2) and utilizes a set of defined transitions based on the input signals. Depending on the current state, the module produces corresponding output values: when in S0, it outputs "01"; in S1, it outputs "10"; and in S2, it outputs "11." State transitions are managed by evaluating specific input conditions, allowing the FSM to control flow between these states based on the provided inputs continuously.
