description:
Design a circuit that performs data interleaving on a given input. The module takes an input vector of specified width and rearranges it into an output vector by interleaving its blocks; specifically, it divides the input into a specified number of blocks and rearranges the bits from each block into the output in a round-robin fashion. This functionality is useful for improving data transmission efficiency and ensuring that data is spread across multiple channels for better performance in communication systems.
module top_module(input [0:width-1] data_in,
   output [0:width-1] data_out);

code:
module top_module(input [0:width-1] data_in,
   output [0:width-1] data_out);// input data width
   parameter width = 8;

   // number of blocks in input data
   parameter num_blocks = 2;

   // width of each block
   localparam step = width / num_blocks;

   // vector of output data
   // Removed the wire declaration for data_out since it's already declared as an output port.

   generate

      genvar 	    i;
      for(i = 0; i < step; i = i + 1)
	begin:blocks

	   genvar j;
	   for(j = 0; j < num_blocks; j = j + 1)
	     begin:bits
		assign data_out[i*num_blocks+j] = data_in[i+j*step];
	     end

	end

   endgenerate

endmodule

